# UTMOS22-strong parity source record (current safety posture: 2026-09-12).
# The legacy checkpoint below is provenance only and is never a CI input.
#
# The §3.1 UTMOS sign-off in docs/license-audit.md was ☑ Commercial by
# yousan on 2026-07-23. This license fact does not authorize loading the
# legacy pickle. As of 2026-09-12 the safe preparation boundary can become
# ready when the tensor-only UTMOS export, its fixed SHA-256, and the committed
# fixture are supplied. Numeric parity remains not-ready until both the
# UTMOS and wav2vec exports have fixed SHA-256 values and safe construction.
#
# Snapshot-pinned to HF space sarulab-speech/UTMOS-demo commit
# 47212055c2ecfb02d40cec2395233b83295d3d30 (== utmos_env_probe.sh's
# requirements.txt pin recorded in decision-memo.md §(iii)); resolving via
# the immutable `resolve/<sha>/` URL guarantees byte-stability even if
# the space's `main` branch later moves.
#
# CKPT_SHA256 MUST match the sha256 recorded in .github/pins.yaml under the
# `utmos22-strong` entry; both were measured 2026-07-17 by campaign-2
# utmos-probe. Editing either side requires editing the other. These legacy
# fields are retained for provenance and are not consumed by parity-utmos.yml.
CKPT_URL=https://huggingface.co/spaces/sarulab-speech/UTMOS-demo/resolve/47212055c2ecfb02d40cec2395233b83295d3d30/epoch=3-step=7459.ckpt
CKPT_SHA256=44c57e3e4135a243b43d2c82b6a693fcd56f15f9ad0e1eb2a8b31fdecd3a49b8

# The CI safe-state-dict boundary is currently disabled because the owner has
# not supplied a fixed tensor-only export and its digest. Supplying these
# values enables preparation-boundary checks only; it does not claim numeric
# reference parity. Do not replace these comments with an URL unless the
# export provenance covers every inference tensor.
# STATE_DICT_URL=https://example.invalid/utmos22-strong.state_dict.safetensors
# STATE_DICT_SHA256=<64 lowercase hex digest>

# Numeric upstream-reference parity has an additional independent input. The
# UTMOS-only preparation boundary may run without these fields, but parity must
# remain blocked until the wav2vec state-dict and its digest are fixed too.
# W2V_STATE_DICT_URL=https://example.invalid/wav2vec_small.state_dict.safetensors
# W2V_STATE_DICT_SHA256=<64 lowercase hex digest>
